      ],
      "description": "The (Vowel + Consonant)உயிர்மெய் எழுத்துக்கள் are compound letters in Tamil formed by combining a consonant (மெய்) with a vowel (உயிர்). For example, the consonant ள்(l) combines with vowels to form ள, ளா, ளி, ளீ, ளு, ளூ, ளெ, ளே, ளை, ளொ, ளோ, and ளௌ."
